.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PTHREAD_CREATE 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pthread_create
.Nm pthread_cancel
.Nm pthread_mutex_lock
.Nd create, cancel and lock threads
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In pthread.h
.Ft int
.Fn pthread_create "pthread_t *thread" "const pthread_attr_t *attr" "void *(*start)(void *)" "void *arg"
.Ft int
.Fn pthread_cancel "pthread_t thread"
.Ft int
.Fn pthread_mutex_lock "pthread_mutex_t *mutex"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions create a thread, request cancellation and acquire a mutex. A
.Ft pthread_t is the thread control-block pointer.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The functions return 0 on success or an error number.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er EAGAIN is returned when a thread cannot be created. .Er EINVAL is returned for an invalid
attribute or mutex. .Er ESRCH is returned for an unknown thread.
.Sh STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2024; ring 1.
.Sh CAVEATS
The thread id is the 30-bit kernel tid; .Ft pthread_t is the TCB pointer. Cancellation is
deferred only. See H-19 and C57.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pthread_create 3
.Xr libc 7
